00:45:25.810 --> 00:45:27.200
Yeah.

00:45:27.200 --> 00:45:27.800
Glad.

00:45:30.700 --> 00:45:32.920
Ed, what was wrong between you and Nick Varner?

00:45:33.880 --> 00:45:35.520
We just had a little misunderstanding.

00:45:36.840 --> 00:45:39.430
Have anything to do with Taylor's murder?

00:45:40.520 --> 00:45:41.340
No, it didn't.

00:45:42.540 --> 00:45:43.580
Do you know who killed Taylor?

00:45:45.940 --> 00:45:46.740
Did Paul kill him?

00:45:47.110 --> 00:45:47.630
Shut up.

00:45:47.950 --> 00:45:48.570
Ed, did he?

00:45:48.860 --> 00:45:50.820
If you must be a nitwit, don't go around with a megaphone.

00:45:54.730 --> 00:45:56.200
Then he did kill him.

00:45:57.350 --> 00:46:00.000
It would be nice if somebody else in this town besides me thought he did.

00:46:01.660 --> 00:46:04.730
It would be especially nice if that somebody were his sister.

00:46:05.610 --> 00:46:07.940
Today's observer practically said he killed him.

00:46:08.580 --> 00:46:10.760
It wouldn't dare print that if it weren't true.

00:46:11.370 --> 00:46:13.880
Listen, Snipp, you know a lot about newspapers.

00:46:14.060 --> 00:46:15.460
Matthew's in with Varna.

00:46:15.580 --> 00:46:17.920
They don't want Paul to win the election.

00:46:18.400 --> 00:46:21.240
What you saw this morning is only a start at what's coming.

00:46:21.700 --> 00:46:25.520
They're gonna rattle Taylor Henry's bones until the final vote's cast.

00:46:26.100 --> 00:46:28.240
You shouldn't mind. Paul doesn't.

00:46:28.420 --> 00:46:29.820
After all, he's a politician.

00:46:30.600 --> 00:46:38.320
Matthews wouldn't print it if it weren't true. He wouldn't snippy wood. I don't believe you and I never will

00:46:38.480 --> 00:47:00.000
You see you a kind of lady as Janet Henry

00:47:00.730 --> 00:47:01.490
Tell her to go away.

00:47:01.850 --> 00:47:03.460
Can't do that. She knows you're better.

00:47:04.460 --> 00:47:05.840
When are we going to be alone again?

00:47:06.400 --> 00:47:08.200
Never. If I can help it.

00:47:08.620 --> 00:47:10.120
I suppose I'll have to see her.

00:47:10.910 --> 00:47:12.670
No wonder people beat you up.

00:47:18.020 --> 00:47:18.600
Come in, please.

00:47:27.890 --> 00:47:29.790
Paul says you're feeling much better, Mr. Beaumont.

00:47:30.410 --> 00:47:32.390
They say I'll be able to sit up by the first of the year.

00:47:33.140 --> 00:47:34.360
Paul says you'll be out in a week.

00:47:35.050 --> 00:47:36.670
Sounds like you've been seeing a lot of Paul.

00:47:38.040 --> 00:47:39.740
Let's don't talk about Paul.

00:47:40.540 --> 00:47:41.700
What do we talk about?

00:47:42.380 --> 00:47:45.450
You comfortable here?

00:47:46.010 --> 00:47:46.630
More or less.

00:47:48.110 --> 00:47:48.650
No fun?

00:47:49.410 --> 00:47:49.890
No fun.

00:47:51.510 --> 00:47:54.670
Hasn't your nurse been treating you well?

00:47:55.730 --> 00:47:56.770
Not as well as I'd like.

00:47:57.670 --> 00:47:58.190
Poor boy.

00:48:00.350 --> 00:48:02.810
If I'd known you were being neglected, I would have come sooner.

00:48:04.430 --> 00:48:07.200
What's this I heard about coming sooner?

00:48:09.430 --> 00:48:13.090
I said if I had known he was recovering so rapidly, I would have come sooner.

00:48:13.800 --> 00:48:16.060
Boy, I figured Ed's lucky for you to come at all.

00:48:16.720 --> 00:48:19.820
Oh, hey, Ed, Janet made me buy these for you.

00:48:19.940 --> 00:48:20.140
Huh?

00:48:21.300 --> 00:48:21.790
Oh.

00:48:23.320 --> 00:48:24.000
Well, how are you?

00:48:24.440 --> 00:48:24.880
Fine.

00:48:25.850 --> 00:48:26.910
How do you like that?

00:48:27.050 --> 00:48:28.460
See what comes from having brains?

00:48:28.760 --> 00:48:30.000
Use your brains instead of your fingers.

00:48:30.030 --> 00:48:31.910
He's always telling me. Look what happened.

00:48:32.190 --> 00:48:34.350
I go about my business, he winds up in the hospital.

00:48:34.510 --> 00:48:35.830
Yeah, but think of the rest I'm getting.

00:48:36.130 --> 00:48:39.310
Yeah. Hey, look.

00:48:39.720 --> 00:48:41.640
How do you like that? Fifteen Gs.

00:48:46.540 --> 00:48:46.940
Congratulations.

00:48:48.050 --> 00:48:48.720
Thanks.

00:48:49.990 --> 00:48:53.070
We're not announcing it until after the election.

00:48:53.690 --> 00:48:58.230
Oh, no? How's everything else going, Paul?

00:48:58.590 --> 00:48:59.110
Oh, fine.

00:48:59.420 --> 00:49:00.000
Keeping slots on the phone.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:02.480
Sure. I'd get him out of town.

00:49:04.390 --> 00:49:06.030
Paul, don't you have to pick up Opal?

00:49:06.700 --> 00:49:07.660
Opal? Oh, no.

00:49:08.070 --> 00:49:09.830
Opal went to the country for the weekend.

00:49:10.320 --> 00:49:10.860
Where in the country?

00:49:11.580 --> 00:49:12.080
I don't know.

00:49:12.520 --> 00:49:14.580
You know, she acted kind of mysterious about it.

00:49:14.820 --> 00:49:16.780
I guess maybe it's just a party or something, though.

00:49:17.200 --> 00:49:18.320
You better run along anyway.

00:49:18.720 --> 00:49:19.760
You have to change for dinner.

00:49:20.280 --> 00:49:21.440
Yeah, yeah. Are you coming?

00:49:21.920 --> 00:49:23.020
I'll be along in a minute.

00:49:23.360 --> 00:49:23.660
Okay.

00:49:24.060 --> 00:49:25.500
That is, if you don't mind my sting.

00:49:25.800 --> 00:49:26.400
Why should I?

00:49:27.630 --> 00:49:29.690
Well, Ed, do you need anything?

00:49:29.690 --> 00:49:30.000
No.

00:49:30.320 --> 00:49:32.820
No, not a thing.

00:49:33.360 --> 00:49:34.140
I'll take these.

00:49:36.200 --> 00:49:37.390
Guess you don't at that.

00:49:41.770 --> 00:49:43.110
Well, I'll see you later.

00:49:43.570 --> 00:49:44.110
Keep punching.

00:49:44.660 --> 00:49:50.320
Do you hate me for this?

00:49:51.490 --> 00:49:52.320
Why should I?

00:49:52.400 --> 00:49:53.360
You're not dishing it out to me.

00:49:55.370 --> 00:49:57.240
You're a strange man.

00:49:58.820 --> 00:49:59.380
Tell me.

00:50:00.030 --> 00:50:04.030
Why did you take such a beating from Nick Vaughn?

00:50:04.030 --> 00:50:06.710
For Paul, on account, he pays me.

00:50:06.710 --> 00:50:08.810
That's no reason.

00:50:08.810 --> 00:50:10.810
Suppose I said he pulled me out of a river once.

00:50:10.810 --> 00:50:12.540
I wouldn't believe you.

00:50:12.540 --> 00:50:18.820
Kate, I did it because he's my friend and he's square, remember?

00:50:18.820 --> 00:50:22.110
And because he would have taken the same beating from me.

00:50:22.110 --> 00:50:27.080
That's what I felt about you, a stubborn loyalty.

00:50:27.080 --> 00:50:28.680
That's why I want you to help me.

00:50:30.190 --> 00:50:30.510
Will you?

00:50:31.700 --> 00:50:32.080
No.

00:50:32.880 --> 00:50:36.810
I don't want you around because I'm liable to start making passes at you.

00:50:38.630 --> 00:50:41.030
Besides, that crummy brother of yours needed killing.

00:50:42.980 --> 00:51:00.000
He was as near crying as anybody could.

00:51:00.000 --> 00:51:02.820
I must be losing my grip.

00:51:02.820 --> 00:51:05.700
I used to put young ladies into hysterics.

00:51:05.700 --> 00:51:12.390
Hey, find out if a guy named Matthews who owns The Observer has a place in the country, will you?

00:51:12.390 --> 00:51:19.670
All right. Thank you very much.

00:51:19.670 --> 00:51:20.670
Here.

00:51:20.670 --> 00:51:30.000
Matthews has a place near Pine Lake.

00:51:30.000 --> 00:51:30.830
- Thanks.

00:51:30.830 --> 00:51:32.290
- You've got your clothes on.

00:51:32.290 --> 00:51:34.180
- Well, I can't very well go out without 'em.

00:51:34.180 --> 00:51:35.180
People might talk.

00:51:35.180 --> 00:51:36.180
- But it's raining out.

00:51:36.180 --> 00:51:37.180
You've got a temperature.

00:51:37.180 --> 00:51:38.180
Dr. Redman will never allow--

00:51:38.180 --> 00:51:39.820
- Send that to Dr. Redman.

00:51:39.820 --> 00:51:41.570
- I'm sorry.

00:52:50.190 --> 00:52:54.350
- Isn't it kinda wet for you to be out there?

00:52:54.350 --> 00:52:57.630
- Rusty, little rubber ball is back.

00:52:57.630 --> 00:52:59.960
I told you you liked the way we bounced 'em around.

00:53:00.120 --> 00:53:01.860
I was wondering where you boys were.

00:53:02.280 --> 00:53:04.860
What do you suppose gives me such a boot out of slugging you?

00:53:05.080 --> 00:53:06.800
Jeff, you talk too much.

00:53:07.300 --> 00:53:07.760
Sit down.

00:53:08.640 --> 00:53:11.300
Won't you take your coat off and dry yourself, Mr. Beaumont?

00:53:13.330 --> 00:53:13.770
Thanks.

00:53:19.220 --> 00:53:20.440
You're Mrs. Matthews, I take it.

00:53:20.580 --> 00:53:21.400
Yes, I am.

00:53:23.160 --> 00:53:25.300
Sit here, Beaumont, where it's nice and warm.

00:53:37.900 --> 00:53:39.040
You feeling all right again, Ed?

00:53:39.280 --> 00:53:40.780
I'm fine, Nick.

00:53:41.210 --> 00:53:41.990
That's good.

00:53:43.120 --> 00:53:44.760
You boys can go back to town tomorrow.

00:53:45.760 --> 00:53:48.980
You see, we were playing safe as long as we didn't know for sure you weren't going to die.

00:53:49.230 --> 00:53:50.830
I'm glad you've come, Mr. Beaumont.

00:53:51.030 --> 00:53:52.450
It's been so dull around here.

00:53:52.550 --> 00:53:54.730
Nobody talking to you and Opal weeping.

00:53:54.870 --> 00:53:55.810
No, Eloise, I...

00:53:55.810 --> 00:53:58.330
Well, you know she's done nothing but weep since she talked with you.

00:53:59.030 --> 00:54:00.000
It's been awful.

00:54:00.510 --> 00:54:02.410
Want me to tell you what they're eating their hearts out about?

00:54:02.660 --> 00:54:03.040
Sure.

00:54:05.160 --> 00:54:07.100
Opal thinks her brother murdered Taylor Henry.

00:54:08.500 --> 00:54:11.810
That's what she's been talking to your husband about.

00:54:11.870 --> 00:54:12.670
She's been telling him that...

00:54:12.670 --> 00:54:13.250
Hey, don't!

00:54:13.660 --> 00:54:16.160
Baby, you're sure one for getting beat up, ain't you?

00:54:16.180 --> 00:54:18.540
Let him talk. It's kind of entertaining.

00:54:21.360 --> 00:54:22.300
Well, Opal, am I right?

00:54:22.680 --> 00:54:23.600
Isn't that what you were doing?

00:54:23.960 --> 00:54:24.280
Please.

00:54:24.970 --> 00:54:25.270
Oh.

00:54:26.670 --> 00:54:30.000
Nobody's supposed to talk about it except you and your brother's other enemy.

00:54:30.700 --> 00:54:31.940
He did murder Taylor.

00:54:33.320 --> 00:54:34.480
You see?

00:54:35.560 --> 00:54:38.080
And of course, your husband is going to print her accusation.

00:54:38.440 --> 00:54:43.650
Not that he believes Paul did the killing, but he's in kind of a tough spot.

00:54:44.660 --> 00:54:47.820
Nick owns the mortgage on The Observer, and he has to do what Nick says.

00:54:47.920 --> 00:54:48.720
Stop it, Beaumont.

00:54:49.130 --> 00:54:49.970
Shut up.

00:54:49.970 --> 00:54:59.280
And so although your husband doesn't believe Paul is guilty, he's going to print the story tomorrow, and it'll carry a lovely wallop.

00:55:00.380 --> 00:55:03.340
You can just picture it in black ink all over the Observer.

00:55:04.290 --> 00:55:07.190
Opal Madvik accuses brother of murder.

00:55:09.980 --> 00:55:12.630
Clyde, is that true?

00:55:12.790 --> 00:55:14.030
Well, I...

00:55:14.030 --> 00:55:15.490
Here's the funniest angle of it all.

00:55:17.040 --> 00:55:20.180
As soon as Nick frames Paul Madvik, he'll let the Observer go bankrupt.

00:55:21.060 --> 00:55:23.390
You see, he doesn't want to be a publisher.

00:55:28.480 --> 00:55:29.910
Does that mean you're broke?

00:55:30.600 --> 00:55:31.980
I'm afraid it does, darling.

00:55:32.750 --> 00:55:34.610
Five years.

00:55:35.050 --> 00:55:36.540
From riches to rags.

00:55:37.360 --> 00:55:39.400
It's been quite a ride, hasn't it?

00:55:39.640 --> 00:55:57.790
Have a drink with me, Mr. Beaumont?

00:55:59.000 --> 00:55:59.400
Sure.

00:56:01.720 --> 00:56:03.900
- All through, Ed?

00:56:03.900 --> 00:56:06.310
- You'd hardly believe how through I am.

00:56:06.310 --> 00:56:08.170
- Well, what does it amount to?

00:56:08.170 --> 00:56:10.370
It's our turn to hang one on you and Paul,

00:56:10.370 --> 00:56:12.950
and we're doing it.

00:56:12.950 --> 00:56:15.260
The girl came here on her own.

00:56:15.260 --> 00:56:17.110
So did Matthews.

00:56:17.110 --> 00:56:18.860
So did you.

00:56:18.860 --> 00:56:20.300
Now, as far as I'm concerned,

00:56:20.300 --> 00:56:23.870
she and you and he can go wherever you wanna go.

00:56:23.870 --> 00:56:25.810
I'm going to bed.

00:56:25.810 --> 00:56:27.670
Come on, boys.

00:56:27.670 --> 00:56:28.510
- Well, wait a minute.

00:56:28.510 --> 00:56:30.000
You mean I don't get to smack back?

00:56:30.000 --> 00:56:31.500
What for?

00:56:31.500 --> 00:56:34.480
He's through as soon as the observer comes out in the morning.

00:56:34.480 --> 00:56:36.530
Good night, Snipp.

00:56:36.530 --> 00:56:43.090
Aren't you coming to bed, dear?

00:56:43.090 --> 00:56:46.070
Here's how.

00:56:46.070 --> 00:56:49.480
Little rubber ball does all right, don't he?

00:57:12.510 --> 00:57:14.660
- Do we have another?

00:57:14.660 --> 00:57:27.450
- Why not?

00:57:27.450 --> 00:57:29.890
- Louise, come upstairs.

00:57:31.210 --> 00:57:33.110
Throw something at him, Mr. Beaumont.

00:57:33.620 --> 00:57:44.880
Why should I go to bed?

00:57:45.760 --> 00:57:47.660
It's much nicer here.

00:57:51.330 --> 00:57:51.770
Which room?

00:57:52.230 --> 00:57:52.530
What?

00:57:52.750 --> 00:57:53.510
His room. Which is it?

00:57:53.820 --> 00:57:54.390
In front.

00:58:17.980 --> 00:58:28.160
close on. Get out of here. Was it Clyde? Yeah. Dead as a mackerel.

00:58:56.940 --> 00:58:58.040
Where you going, Ed?

00:58:58.040 --> 00:59:00.000
Thought I'd get a little fresher.

00:59:00.000 --> 00:59:07.910
I was thinking it's kind of funny that with an opening quote on the pen on the table we didn't find any writing up there.

00:59:07.910 --> 00:59:11.390
What, no writing? We'll have to discuss that sometime.

00:59:11.390 --> 00:59:12.760
Rusty.

00:59:12.760 --> 00:59:16.020
This is my pigeon.

00:59:16.020 --> 00:59:22.180
Hiya, big brain. See what I mean?

00:59:22.180 --> 00:59:23.110
Hey, the party ain't over.

00:59:23.110 --> 00:59:30.000
We're going home.

00:59:30.000 --> 00:59:32.710
We're going out of here, Paul. If you want to stop us, try.

00:59:32.850 --> 00:59:34.960
Thanks. Let him go.

00:59:37.270 --> 00:59:37.610
Beat it.

00:59:40.450 --> 00:59:42.980
Hey, take your sleeping beauty with you.

00:59:49.160 --> 00:59:51.180
You ain't the only one who gets action on our team, huh?

00:59:52.540 --> 00:59:54.130
Matthews just committed suicide.

00:59:54.740 --> 00:59:55.760
Matthews? Here?

00:59:56.290 --> 00:59:59.870
Yeah. Listen, the Observer's loaded with dynamite for the morning.

01:00:00.860 --> 01:00:04.320
Get Judge Thomas on the phone and have him appoint somebody close to us to administer the estate.

01:00:04.600 --> 01:00:05.760
He can do it because there's no will.

01:00:06.490 --> 01:00:07.970
And have the administrator kill the story.

01:00:08.740 --> 01:00:09.040
Get it?

01:00:09.260 --> 01:00:09.540
Yeah.

01:00:09.940 --> 01:00:10.900
Come on, fella, do it, will you?

01:00:11.170 --> 01:00:18.690
But, Paul, I can't make my boys vote the reform ticket.

01:00:18.810 --> 01:00:19.230
Why not?

01:00:19.520 --> 01:00:21.040
Most of them come from a reform school.

01:00:25.810 --> 01:00:26.670
Hey, Ingrid, how are you?

01:00:26.690 --> 01:00:28.190
Okay, we'll give the stuff to Murphy and Kelly.

01:00:29.190 --> 01:00:30.000
Hey, look, you're not supposed to.

01:00:30.000 --> 01:00:31.800
I thought you were supposed to stay in bed.

01:00:32.000 --> 01:00:33.300
I just got a tip from Farr's office.

01:00:33.500 --> 01:00:34.800
It's gonna bring you in for questioning.

01:00:35.000 --> 01:00:36.300
Take it easy, will ya?

01:00:36.500 --> 01:00:38.840
What can that overstuffed Pelican question me about,

01:00:39.040 --> 01:00:40.340
now we got the Observer shut up?

01:00:40.540 --> 01:00:43.270
- What about Sloss? - Tut.

01:00:43.560 --> 01:00:46.170
- Yes, Paul? - Donovan and Burns are out picking them up now.

01:00:46.370 --> 01:00:48.670
- They ought to be in any minute. - You got Sloss's ticket?

01:00:48.870 --> 01:00:49.670
- Yes, Paul. - Good.

01:00:49.870 --> 01:00:53.580
I'm sending him up to Maine for a nice long rest.

01:00:53.780 --> 01:00:55.630
I wouldn't be too sure about Farr.

01:00:55.830 --> 01:00:58.120
Been needled by some more of those anonymous letters.

01:00:58.320 --> 01:01:00.000
He doesn't think much of the ticket.

01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:03.520
- I think it's the chances. - Well, you don't, huh?

01:01:03.520 --> 01:01:08.080
Maybe I better go down and give that beatle nose a little pep talk.

01:01:08.080 --> 01:01:09.970
Yeah, wait a minute.

01:01:09.970 --> 01:01:12.220
- Look, you feel strong enough to come along? - Sure.

01:01:12.220 --> 01:01:16.330
- Let's go. - What's that?

01:01:16.330 --> 01:01:20.460
Yes? When Sloss gets here, put in my office and see that nobody gets to him.

01:01:20.460 --> 01:01:20.840
Sorry.

01:01:33.230 --> 01:01:37.400
Hiya Sloss, peg him up to Tuttle.

01:01:37.400 --> 01:01:45.400
- Why, it's Sloss! - That came from your window, Paul.

01:01:45.400 --> 01:01:46.550
- Let me get pictures. - Come on.

01:02:05.120 --> 01:02:05.820
No use, Paul.

01:02:06.120 --> 01:02:07.380
You'd have gotten out six different ways.

01:02:11.810 --> 01:02:12.850
Yes, you're right.

01:02:20.670 --> 01:02:22.390
I suppose they'll pin this one on me, too.

01:02:23.570 --> 01:02:24.170
Why not?

01:02:24.940 --> 01:02:25.940
Sloss was the big witness.

01:02:26.060 --> 01:02:27.800
No one had a better reason to get rid of him than you.

01:02:29.240 --> 01:02:30.000
Paul, you got to get rid of him.

01:02:30.000 --> 01:02:32.260
Go to Farah and tell him all you know about the Taylor Henry murder.

01:02:33.500 --> 01:02:35.550
Think up something else.

01:02:36.660 --> 01:02:37.660
Are you covering up for someone?

01:02:37.880 --> 01:02:38.280
No.

01:02:38.860 --> 01:02:39.720
Well, then you better talk.

01:02:40.280 --> 01:02:41.420
I can't talk.

01:02:41.690 --> 01:02:42.210
Why not?

01:02:44.560 --> 01:02:47.890
I killed Taylor Henry.

01:02:51.940 --> 01:02:56.550
Tell me how it happened.

01:02:57.160 --> 01:02:58.120
It was an accident.

01:02:59.090 --> 01:03:00.000
He was at the house when I was...

01:03:00.000 --> 01:03:04.770
talking with old man henry about opal and him followed me down the street and started the

01:03:04.770 --> 01:03:10.890
argument all over again took a poke at me i smacked him and he fell and crushed his skull

01:03:10.890 --> 01:03:18.670
on the curb certainly gummed things up keeping quiet all this time why did you you had a perfect

01:03:18.670 --> 01:03:25.790
self-defense plea i didn't want that i want janet henry i don't want her more than i've ever wanted

01:03:25.790 --> 01:03:30.000
anything in my life what chance would i have with her if she knew that you had more chance

01:03:30.000 --> 01:03:33.490
More chance then than you have now. More chance of beating the rap, too.

01:03:33.490 --> 01:03:35.860
Farrah'll never touch me.

01:03:35.860 --> 01:03:39.800
Listen, if he thought it would do him any good, he'd arrest his own mother and get a conviction.

01:03:39.800 --> 01:03:42.200
And those letters have got him plenty worried.

01:04:46.570 --> 01:04:53.510
so. Put up with Paul. Be polite

01:04:53.510 --> 01:04:55.800
to him. For the sake of the political backing

01:04:55.800 --> 01:04:57.690
her father needed. That was easy.

01:04:58.660 --> 01:05:00.000
Then she decided Paul killed her

01:05:00.000 --> 01:05:05.180
Her brother was going to escape punishment, but even then she played along.

01:05:05.180 --> 01:05:09.620
That's splendid. Paul's sister and his sweetheart both trying to steer him into the electric chair.

01:05:09.620 --> 01:05:13.830
He certainly has a lot of luck with his women, doesn't he?

01:05:13.830 --> 01:05:18.330
I wrote those letters. I'm sure Paul killed Taylor, and I'm going to prove it.

01:05:18.330 --> 01:05:22.310
What do you think Paul's going to do when I tell him about all this?

01:05:22.310 --> 01:05:26.970
You're not going to tell him. What good would it do?

01:05:26.970 --> 01:05:29.800
Besides, you're too fond of him to hurt him.

01:05:31.790 --> 01:05:32.670
There's another reason.

01:05:33.590 --> 01:05:35.330
I'm asking you not to.

01:05:37.820 --> 01:05:41.800
Can't you forget about Paul for a minute?

01:05:42.490 --> 01:05:44.010
I thought we'd settled all that.

01:05:45.200 --> 01:05:48.130
I told you once Paul wouldn't make any difference if I wanted you.

01:05:49.010 --> 01:05:50.210
But I don't.

01:05:51.780 --> 01:05:54.780
You still think you're five points better than Paul and four better than me.

01:05:56.590 --> 01:05:57.150
No, I'm not.

01:06:00.120 --> 01:06:03.180
Now that we understand each other, let's get out of here.

01:06:05.350 --> 01:06:07.190
X-Strave, read all about it.

01:06:07.540 --> 01:06:08.540
X-Strave, paper.

01:06:12.350 --> 01:06:16.070
Hi, Jim.

01:06:23.470 --> 01:06:24.810
Hi, Ed.

01:06:25.710 --> 01:06:30.000
Well, looks like you was right about that swivel.

01:06:30.000 --> 01:07:00.000
Neck far really been putting it to you, haven't they? Did he get that indictment? Yeah, don't you worry. We're getting rid of habeas corpus. There ain't a judge in this town that'll hold me. Any judge will hold you if you don't come through with the truth. Oh, you too, huh? Did you have Sloss bumped off? No. What about Taylor? I told you about that. Yeah, you told me. You told me you were

01:07:00.000 --> 01:07:01.320
keeping quiet for Janet Henry.

01:07:01.900 --> 01:07:02.740
Well, that's crazy.

01:07:03.710 --> 01:07:04.970
She doesn't even like you.

01:07:05.150 --> 01:07:06.390
Don't start that again.

01:07:07.080 --> 01:07:07.800
I'm telling you.

01:07:08.140 --> 01:07:09.960
She's been trying to shove you into the electric chair

01:07:09.960 --> 01:07:12.340
by writing anonymous letters to Farr and everybody else.

01:07:12.340 --> 01:07:13.100
That's enough.

01:07:14.880 --> 01:07:15.700
What is this, Ed?

01:07:16.230 --> 01:07:18.500
You're trying to get her for yourself.

01:07:19.500 --> 01:07:20.140
I'm tired.

01:07:20.280 --> 01:07:21.280
Go on, get out of here.

01:07:21.760 --> 01:07:23.080
I'll get out when I finish talking.

01:07:24.620 --> 01:07:25.960
You'll get out when you're told to.

01:07:26.430 --> 01:07:27.890
This is the kiss-off.

01:07:28.520 --> 01:07:29.200
Okay, Paul.

01:07:29.200 --> 01:07:29.380
Come on.

01:07:35.600 --> 01:07:36.060
Say, Ed.

01:07:36.420 --> 01:07:36.720
Yeah?

01:07:37.260 --> 01:07:38.460
I took your advice.

01:07:38.900 --> 01:07:39.940
I got that bicycle.

01:07:41.250 --> 01:07:42.330
My kid's riding it.

01:07:43.160 --> 01:07:43.600
Ha, ha, ha.

01:08:00.060 --> 01:08:14.630
thought the day you left me behind take a stroll and get you right off my mind

01:08:14.630 --> 01:08:30.000
but now I live out the sunshine why you have to turn

01:08:36.970 --> 01:08:39.080
Oh, come right up. Give me another one.

01:08:50.560 --> 01:08:54.130
If it ain't sock me again, boomer!

01:09:06.620 --> 01:09:11.400
- Hello, Jeff. - Hey, gang.

01:09:11.900 --> 01:09:15.770
Meet the swellest guy I ever skinned a knuckle on.

01:09:16.960 --> 01:09:20.420
- We're gonna have a little drink. - Okay.

01:09:23.620 --> 01:09:26.020
No, not wet days, Muggs.

01:09:26.970 --> 01:09:29.270
I got just a place for me and you.

01:09:31.660 --> 01:09:35.960
A little room upstairs that's too small for you to fall down in.

01:09:35.960 --> 01:09:38.580
I can bounce you around off the walls.

01:09:38.580 --> 01:09:43.320
That way, we won't be wasting a lot of time while you get up off the floor.

01:09:43.320 --> 01:09:46.850
Excuse us, gents.

01:09:46.850 --> 01:09:49.380
We gotta go up and play handball.

01:09:49.380 --> 01:09:52.440
Me and Cuddles.

01:09:52.440 --> 01:09:58.960
Sit down.

01:10:05.760 --> 01:10:07.980
Go on, sit in any chair you want to sit in.

01:10:08.320 --> 01:10:10.610
If you don't like that one, take another one.

01:10:11.210 --> 01:10:13.590
I want you to consider yourself my guest.

01:10:14.580 --> 01:10:20.110
We'll have a couple of drinks, and then I'm going to knock your teeth out.

01:10:20.550 --> 01:10:21.750
Nothing wrong with this chair.

01:10:22.010 --> 01:10:22.910
You're a liar.

01:10:23.860 --> 01:10:25.940
There ain't a chair in this dump worth of time.

01:10:26.630 --> 01:10:26.970
Look.

01:10:26.970 --> 01:10:27.490
Look.

01:10:31.790 --> 01:10:36.160
See, Beaumont, you don't know a cockeyed thing about chairs.

01:10:37.810 --> 01:10:38.350
My hair.

01:10:39.280 --> 01:10:42.090
Ah, a wise guy.

01:10:43.620 --> 01:10:45.480
You think I'm drunk?

01:10:46.210 --> 01:10:47.370
No, you're not drunk.

01:10:47.670 --> 01:10:48.590
I am drunk.

01:10:49.330 --> 01:10:50.710
I'm drunker than you are.

01:10:51.120 --> 01:10:53.270
I'm drunker than anybody in this dump.

01:11:00.730 --> 01:11:01.670
What'll it be, gents?

01:11:01.770 --> 01:11:02.690
Where you been?

01:11:03.170 --> 01:11:05.110
I rung for you an hour ago.

01:11:06.800 --> 01:11:11.060
I bring the best friend I got in the world up here for a drink.

01:11:11.840 --> 01:11:15.500
And we gotta sit around waiting a half an hour for a broken-down waiter.

01:11:15.790 --> 01:11:16.340
What do you want?

01:11:17.240 --> 01:11:17.620
Dry.

01:11:18.420 --> 01:11:19.140
Scotch.

01:11:22.540 --> 01:11:26.040
And don't get the idea I don't know what you're up to either.

01:11:26.580 --> 01:11:27.730
I'm not up to anything.

01:11:28.420 --> 01:11:30.000
I'd like to see Nick and so...

01:11:30.060 --> 01:11:31.100
I thought I'd find him here.

01:11:31.260 --> 01:11:32.120
That's a lie.

01:11:32.280 --> 01:11:33.780
You don't care where Nick is.

01:11:34.130 --> 01:11:35.170
It's me you're after.

01:11:35.560 --> 01:11:35.860
No.

01:11:36.360 --> 01:11:37.980
I know what you're up to.

01:11:38.760 --> 01:11:40.700
You're a heel, that's what you are.

01:11:41.400 --> 01:11:42.760
You know what I'm gonna do?

01:11:43.410 --> 01:11:46.520
I'm gonna beat the hide off of you.

01:12:00.320 --> 01:12:09.050
you right here i'd have it your way do you think it's a smart trick coming up here and trying to

01:12:09.050 --> 01:12:15.040
get me to talk about what sloss you know what i think about that guy you want to get a medal

01:12:15.040 --> 01:12:27.200
how'd it happen oh no wise guy little jeff ain't talking about that why not a secret yeah a secret

01:12:27.200 --> 01:12:29.910
between me and nick

01:12:30.280 --> 01:12:36.200
and the lamppost, and you ain't no lamppost, you're a hale.

01:12:36.200 --> 01:12:43.220
- Buy a drink. - Ain't a bad idea.

01:12:43.220 --> 01:12:56.540
But you're still a hale, and I'm still gonna knock your block off.

01:12:56.540 --> 01:12:59.250
Don't worry about me.

01:13:00.000 --> 01:13:04.450
- Nick's got everything fixed.

01:13:04.450 --> 01:13:05.290
- Right.

01:13:05.290 --> 01:13:07.880
- Scotch.

01:13:07.880 --> 01:13:10.370
- I wouldn't bank too much on Nick.

01:13:10.370 --> 01:13:12.410
Remember he let McMurray fry.

01:13:12.410 --> 01:13:14.920
- Well, I'm not McMurray.

01:13:14.920 --> 01:13:18.800
A swell chance with all I got on Nick.

01:13:18.800 --> 01:13:20.870
- What have you got on him?

01:13:24.170 --> 01:13:26.980
- He thinks I'm drunk enough to tell him.

01:13:26.980 --> 01:13:28.740
- Go on, tell him, Jeff.

01:13:30.480 --> 01:13:35.090
Hi, Nick. Meet Mr. Beaumont. He's a heel.

01:13:35.640 --> 01:13:37.460
I told you to stay undercover.

01:13:37.780 --> 01:13:39.860
This whole joint's undercover, ain't it?

01:13:40.960 --> 01:13:41.600
Oh, Beaumont.

01:13:41.890 --> 01:13:42.530
Hiya, Nick.

01:13:43.090 --> 01:13:43.730
Much out of him?

01:13:44.550 --> 01:13:45.530
No, not much.

01:13:47.400 --> 01:13:49.220
I think you're a pair of heels.

01:13:50.270 --> 01:13:51.450
They've had enough.

01:13:51.880 --> 01:13:52.400
Scotch!

01:13:59.470 --> 01:14:00.000
You talk.

01:14:00.030 --> 01:14:01.770
- You talk too much with your mouth, Jeff.

01:14:01.770 --> 01:14:04.860
I told you that before.

01:14:04.860 --> 01:14:06.390
- What's the matter with you?

01:14:06.390 --> 01:14:07.690
- I'm talking to you, Jeff.

01:14:07.690 --> 01:14:09.340
- Well, quit talking to me.

01:14:09.340 --> 01:14:10.480
- You know we're coming to a place

01:14:10.480 --> 01:14:13.060
where I am gonna quit talking to you.

01:14:13.060 --> 01:14:16.340
- Don't be a heel, Nick.

01:14:16.340 --> 01:14:18.740
You're just burned because I killed Sloss.

01:14:18.740 --> 01:14:22.260
- Sit down and shut up.

01:14:22.260 --> 01:14:24.070
- Don't bore me.

01:14:37.360 --> 01:14:38.430
- Mr. Roscoe?

01:14:38.430 --> 01:14:39.270
- Yeah.

01:14:39.270 --> 01:14:41.180
- Now you see what we gotta do?

01:14:41.180 --> 01:14:47.710
We gotta give him the works.

01:14:47.710 --> 01:14:48.880
- Take it easy, Jeff.

01:15:00.920 --> 01:15:02.880
I'm just a big, good-natured slob.

01:15:04.760 --> 01:15:07.060
Anybody can push me around all they want to,

01:15:07.980 --> 01:15:10.940
and I never do anything about it.

01:15:13.060 --> 01:15:26.770
Let's blow.

01:15:28.070 --> 01:15:29.120
Give me the Roscoe.

01:15:32.200 --> 01:15:34.100
What kind of a heel are you?

01:15:34.100 --> 01:15:35.290
Sit down.

01:15:35.290 --> 01:15:42.190
Sit down.

01:15:42.190 --> 01:15:47.170
Remember, I owe you something.

01:15:47.170 --> 01:15:48.150
Put your hands on the table.

01:15:48.150 --> 01:15:53.720
What a half-smart guy you turned out to be.

01:16:00.440 --> 01:16:01.350
Get the cops.

01:16:01.350 --> 01:16:05.270
Better get a doctor, too, in case Von is not dead.

01:16:05.270 --> 01:16:08.690
Better get an undertaker in case he is.

01:16:10.110 --> 01:16:16.760
All right, boys.

01:16:16.760 --> 01:16:18.030
Put 'em on ice.

01:16:18.030 --> 01:16:19.240
Hold it a minute.

01:16:19.240 --> 01:16:25.940
So long, sweetheart.

01:16:30.570 --> 01:16:37.920
funny man, huh? Yeah, you're going to die laughing. All right, boys, the show's all over. Clear up.

01:16:38.670 --> 01:16:43.850
That was pretty slick, Ed, pinning that slush killing on Jeff. Thanks for giving me those bobs.

01:16:47.010 --> 01:16:52.310
Tell me your wife's folks live in Omaha. Yeah, they got a nice, quiet little place up there. I like it.

01:16:52.910 --> 01:17:00.000
Better wire them that you and the missus are on the way. What is this, a rib? Just a piece of pretty good

01:17:00.000 --> 01:17:07.480
advice? Well, I don't get it. Why don't you get smart? Tomorrow, Paul's going to beat that indictment

01:17:07.480 --> 01:17:12.540
you hung on him, and the first guy he reaches for is going to be you. In a pig's ear, he'll beat it.

01:17:14.790 --> 01:17:22.420
But when he nails your ears over the courthouse door, don't say I didn't warn you. Hey, Ed,

01:17:22.780 --> 01:17:30.000
Ed, wait a minute. Ed, wait, wait. Now, look, I'm not arguing. See? All I'm asking

01:17:30.000 --> 01:17:35.290
is how is Paul going to beat the rap? Will you listen to me or do I have to write it down?

01:17:35.980 --> 01:17:38.740
In the first place, there isn't a judge on the bench who dare hold Paul now if this last thing

01:17:38.740 --> 01:17:43.470
is cleared up. Well, but... And in the second place, and hold on to this one, it wasn't Paul

01:17:43.470 --> 01:17:48.130
that killed young Henry. Hey, how did you figure that out? By that talk I had with him in the

01:17:48.130 --> 01:17:55.310
Huskow. We got down to cases and he told me he did it. But that don't add up. Look, Rummy, it adds

01:17:55.310 --> 01:18:00.000
up swell. If Paul had done it, he wouldn't wait until now to tell me. He's covering up for someone, taking

01:18:00.000 --> 01:18:02.210
taking it for someone extra special.

01:18:02.210 --> 01:18:04.610
If you'll do like I tell you, we'll make the pinch

01:18:04.610 --> 01:18:06.610
and you can postpone that trip to Omaha.

01:18:06.610 --> 01:18:16.730
Say, Ed, are you sure you know what you're talking about?

01:18:16.730 --> 01:18:21.620
You know what I was talking about

01:18:21.620 --> 01:18:26.420
when I brought in Jeff, didn't I?

01:18:26.420 --> 01:18:29.380
Yeah. Well, what are you...

01:18:30.960 --> 01:18:33.490
- What do you want me to do? - Swear to warn for murder.

01:18:33.490 --> 01:18:47.150
- Where's the party? - Janet Henry.

01:18:47.150 --> 01:18:50.460
- Janet Henry. - Janet Henry!

01:18:50.460 --> 01:18:54.660
Why, that's the old man's daughter. That's young Taylor's sister.

01:18:54.660 --> 01:18:57.540
- Why, that's the girl... - That's the girl that Paul's been covering up for.

01:18:57.540 --> 01:18:59.410
Oh, well, I couldn't do...

01:19:00.000 --> 01:19:01.760
I got it on her like a carload of bricks.

01:19:02.010 --> 01:19:03.710
It started when she jumped her brother about Opal

01:19:03.810 --> 01:19:05.610
and ended up with young Henry where they found him.

01:19:05.800 --> 01:19:08.320
All along, Paul's known she did it and he's been covering up for her.

01:19:08.440 --> 01:19:11.460
And all along, she's hated Paul's guts and hated him for himself

01:19:11.560 --> 01:19:13.350
and for the stranglehold he had on the family.

01:19:13.600 --> 01:19:15.970
She's the one that's been circulating those poison pen letters,

01:19:16.060 --> 01:19:19.160
running off the mouth of Matthews, trying to shove Paul into the electric chair.

01:19:19.370 --> 01:19:21.700
I tell you, it's got to be her, just to get busy.

01:19:23.820 --> 01:19:26.850
So you're not talking about just ordinary people, Ed.

01:19:28.030 --> 01:19:29.410
This is Janet Henry.

01:19:32.040 --> 01:19:37.410
- I want no part of it. - Better had far.

01:19:37.410 --> 01:19:40.930
There's only one guy that ever kicked Paul in the pants and got away with it.

01:19:40.930 --> 01:19:43.410
McCloskey, remember?

01:19:43.410 --> 01:19:47.800
And he jumped 18 floors into Center Street before Paul got at him.

01:20:06.840 --> 01:20:07.340
What is it?

01:20:07.490 --> 01:20:08.170
I want to see Miss Henry.

01:20:08.250 --> 01:20:08.890
At this time of night?

01:20:09.050 --> 01:20:09.610
Yeah, at this time of night.

01:20:09.610 --> 01:20:10.690
I couldn't possibly disturb.

01:20:10.970 --> 01:20:11.730
He's out of the question.

01:20:11.810 --> 01:20:12.430
You can't possibly.

01:20:12.770 --> 01:20:13.230
I can't.

01:20:13.290 --> 01:20:14.130
You can't come in here.

01:20:14.230 --> 01:20:15.070
What is it, Peter?

01:20:15.150 --> 01:20:15.630
What's the matter?

01:20:16.260 --> 01:20:16.540
Beaumont.

01:20:16.840 --> 01:20:17.540
I want to see your daughter.

01:20:17.720 --> 01:20:19.080
I'm afraid you're overstepping yourself.

01:20:19.180 --> 01:20:19.880
Get her down here.

01:20:19.920 --> 01:20:21.060
I'll go up and drag her out of bed.

01:20:21.200 --> 01:20:22.440
I'd better call the peace, Mr. Henry.

01:20:22.660 --> 01:20:23.400
You don't have to.

01:20:23.620 --> 01:20:24.340
They're already here.

01:20:24.520 --> 01:20:24.780
What?

01:20:25.390 --> 01:20:27.120
You're going to get her or will I have to?

01:20:27.160 --> 01:20:29.260
Ed, what is it?

01:20:29.340 --> 01:20:30.000
Okay, father.

01:20:30.000 --> 01:20:33.470
Well, I don't know, Ed, now. I've...

01:20:33.470 --> 01:20:35.470
Mr. Farr, I must ask you to explain this intrusion.

01:20:35.470 --> 01:20:38.550
You see, Mr. Henry, it was like this.

01:20:38.550 --> 01:20:40.540
Ed, what does this mean?

01:20:40.540 --> 01:20:42.910
It means Farr has a warrant for your arrest.

01:20:42.910 --> 01:20:46.800
Arrest? What for?

01:20:46.800 --> 01:20:49.680
For the murder of your brother. Why, man, you're crazy.

01:20:49.680 --> 01:20:50.680
You'll have to prove it.

01:20:50.680 --> 01:20:51.600
That's absurd.

01:20:51.600 --> 01:20:54.600
On whose evidence was this preposterous warrant issued?

01:20:54.600 --> 01:20:57.490
My evidence. And, brother, it's hot.

01:21:04.480 --> 01:21:08.460
- Okay, Farr, take her along.

01:21:08.460 --> 01:21:09.880
- All right, go on up to the sandbar

01:21:09.880 --> 01:21:11.040
when she gets her clothes.

01:21:11.040 --> 01:21:12.830
- Wait.

01:21:12.830 --> 01:21:15.910
I think, Mr. Farr, you'd better prepare another warrant.

01:21:15.910 --> 01:21:18.910
I'm the one you want.

01:21:18.910 --> 01:21:22.230
I killed my son.

01:21:22.230 --> 01:21:25.480
I, I followed Taylor and Paul

01:21:25.480 --> 01:21:28.260
after they'd coiled here at the house.

01:21:28.260 --> 01:21:29.640
I caught up with them in the street.

01:21:30.600 --> 01:21:36.430
told Taylor that he was ruining my political career. He struck me. He was going to strike

01:21:36.430 --> 01:21:48.390
again. Well, we scuffled. Somehow he fell and his head hit the curb. When Paul and I

01:21:48.390 --> 01:22:00.000
lifted him up, he was dead. It was an accident. And Paul, I made him promise not to say anything.

01:22:06.750 --> 01:22:07.450
I was getting worried.

01:22:08.790 --> 01:22:10.790
Afraid we'd have to hang the girl to make the old man crack.

01:22:16.870 --> 01:22:18.290
I'm glad to see you beat it, Paul.

01:22:18.510 --> 01:22:20.230
I got the other thing with the frame, eh, Paul?

01:22:20.310 --> 01:22:21.850
He'll pack the old water, Paul.

01:22:21.950 --> 01:22:22.710
Okay, drag him back.

01:22:22.790 --> 01:22:23.590
Well, I'll see you later.

01:22:23.690 --> 01:22:25.010
Who are you going to run for governor in place of Henry?

01:22:25.170 --> 01:22:28.170
I haven't picked him yet, but whoever it is, you can bet on him for a winner.

01:22:28.350 --> 01:22:28.730
That's right.

01:22:42.160 --> 01:22:43.160
Nobody goes first.

01:22:43.160 --> 01:22:48.560
Yes, sir.

01:22:48.560 --> 01:22:49.520
I had to come.

01:22:49.520 --> 01:22:54.150
I want you to take me with you.

01:22:54.150 --> 01:22:59.510
There's no use pretending.

01:23:00.320 --> 01:23:01.500
You love me and you know it.

01:23:02.690 --> 01:23:04.350
No matter what you'd say to the contrary,

01:23:05.750 --> 01:23:07.210
there'd always be something inside of me

01:23:07.210 --> 01:23:08.250
that would say you were lying.

01:23:10.720 --> 01:23:13.180
But Paul...

01:23:13.180 --> 01:23:14.260
No, I didn't.

01:23:15.260 --> 01:23:16.390
You owe him plenty.

01:23:17.350 --> 01:23:18.670
Paul's been fine.

01:23:21.040 --> 01:23:23.040
And in my heart, I'll always be grateful to him.

01:23:24.200 --> 01:23:26.030
But if I married him,

01:23:26.090 --> 01:23:27.970
gratitude would be all I'd have for him.

01:23:31.660 --> 01:23:32.800
The answer is still no.

01:23:34.480 --> 01:23:36.620
Still leaves us on different sides of the tracks.

01:23:38.270 --> 01:23:39.870
Let's dynamite those tracks.

01:23:50.560 --> 01:23:51.640
Take me with you.

01:24:04.410 --> 01:24:05.860
You two got it bad, huh?

01:24:05.860 --> 01:24:11.840
What are you waiting for, you goon?

01:24:11.840 --> 01:24:14.950
Are you kidding?

01:24:14.950 --> 01:24:17.350
What do you want me to do, run out and bring you a preacher?

01:24:17.350 --> 01:24:19.880
Come on, get going before I change my mind.

01:24:19.880 --> 01:24:23.330
Hey!

01:24:32.140 --> 01:24:33.520
I suppose you think I'm nuts.

01:24:35.450 --> 01:24:36.050
Now, the other one.

01:24:39.950 --> 01:24:43.320
If you figure I'm getting married with my rock, you're nuts.
